Sync 2 Google Drives Using RClone - https://youtu.be/BgD5b2MExeE
Download rclone
Extract rclone using Winrar or 7zip
Open the extracted file
Double click the search bar at the top of your file explorer
Type "cmd" and hit enter
Type "rclone config" in the command prompt that opened
Type "n" for a new remote
Type in whatever name you want I used ex
Hit enter on Client ID
Hit enter on Client Secret
Type "1" on Scope
Hit enter on Root_Folder_ID
Hit enter on edit advanced config
Hit enter on Use auto config
Chose your Google account
Press Allow (rclone is safe do not worry)
If you are using a shared drive like I am then type "y" if no type "n"
Then type the number corresponding with the drive you want to select (I chose 3 which is the drive named z2 on my account)
Press enter on the Is this ok?

Do the same thing again.

After you are done with that you can press Q and type in "rclone sync (name of ur remote mine was ex): (name of your second remote): 
it should look something like rclone sync ex: ex2:
Then hit enter and wait for the list to update
Go check your drives and they should have synced :)

